  "notes": "Historical catalog year 2025, extracted via bulletin_scraper.py. Unverified codes: []. Agroecology Option from bulletin page. [REVIEWER FIX 2026-09-18]: This historical plan as originally built could not schedule CHEM 110/111 (concurrent-blocked), STAT 200 (also needs MATH 21), and SOILS 402 (needs CHEM 110) because CHEM 110's real prereq (MATH 22, which itself needs only MATH 21 -- confirmed via planner_engine's own catalog, MATH 21 has no prereq of its own) was never added as an explicit item, unlike PLSCI-2026.json which already carries this exact fix (MATH 21 in Semester 3, MATH 22 in Semester 4 there). The original self-report for this batch attributed the gap entirely to 'the bulletin requirements genuinely changed' and left it unfixed as historically accurate; that is only half right -- the underlying MATH 22 prereq is the SAME systemic gap already fixed in this major's own 2026 file and documented across many other CHEM-110-requiring plans in this repo, not a genuine per-year curriculum difference. Added MATH 21 (Semester 1) and MATH 22 (Semester 2) to close it. Re-verified with build_full_plan (same-era start_year/today) -- 0 scheduling warnings after the fix. [REVIEWER FIX 2026-09-18]: Removed \"MATH 22\" from the Semester 1 math-options bucket. Leaving it there alongside the new dedicated MATH 22 item (Semester 2, added to unlock CHEM 110) caused a real planner_engine.py bug: plan_progress() recomputes which course satisfies which item from scratch every simulated term, in plan order, and a course code shared between two DIFFERENT course-type items gets greedily claimed by whichever item lists it earliest among the still-completed options -- once MATH 22 was actually completed, the bucket item (already legitimately satisfied by MATH 41) re-attributed itself to MATH 22 instead (since MATH 22 was first in ITS OWN option list and now also completed), which left the dedicated MATH 22 item permanently unclaimed and made build_full_plan loop forever re-proposing an already-completed MATH 22 every remaining term (hit the 24-term simulation cap instead of finishing). This is a real planner_engine.py scheduling bug (flagged for the engine reviewers, not patched here) -- the JSON-side fix is to not offer the same course code as options on two separate course items in the first place. MATH 26, MATH 41/40, MATH 110, and MATH 140 remain valid alternatives for this bucket. Re-verified with build_full_plan -- 0 scheduling warnings after the fix.",
